0..76 Comment "// A recursive definition marks each call to itself: `f[<]` descends, `f[>]`"
77..122 Comment "// produces, and an unmarked call is refused."
123..125 Comment "//"
126..201 Comment "// A mark states why the recursion ends or stays productive, so the checker"
202..267 Comment "// trusts no call it cannot classify. An unmarked call is refused"
268..295 Comment "// `UnmarkedSelfReference`."
296..298 Comment "//"
299..368 Comment "// The checker reads each call\'s mark against the definition\'s staged"
369..447 Comment "// parameter. A descent with no parameter, or a production outside a copattern"
448..469 Comment "// block, is refused."
470..472 Comment "//"
473..500 Comment "// - see: #626 — `varied`"
501..527 Comment "// - see: #644 — `ahead`"
528..566 Comment "// - see: #1499 — `constant`, `spin`"
